                        "recommendationid": "235677418",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561199697515582",
                            "num_reviews": 1,
                            "playtime_forever": 3976,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 3976,
                            "last_played": 1784310471
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "As an Italian fan, Sio's humor never disappoints. After getting 100% of the achievements, here's my take:\r\n\r\nI've known Sio's Scottecs series ever since I was a preteen: I've bought all of his Scottecs Megazines, all the currently available Scottecs Gigazines, and a lot of merch in general just to enjoy his simplistic art style and absurdly unpredictable sense of humor. Seeing the game adaptation from Studio Evil made me quite satisfied: not only did they include all of the main characters that appear in the comics, but also stayed truthful to the events and never-ending gags, like the number 7 being the maximum measurement for anything.\r\n\r\nGameplay-wise this game is a bit confusing: maps are not that accurate and it's easy to get lost without a proper sense of direction. Furthermore, the spring mechanic allows you to unknowingly skip some sections of the map and land in a later section of the same area, which is funny to me. However, the vast range of armor, weapons and secrets scattered throughout the levels makes it all worth it: playstyle changes continuously and doesn't get that repetitive as you are fighting, the skill tree grants unique abilities and you can EAT ROCKS to heal, which is crazy.\r\n\r\nIn the end I liked it for its nonsensical humor and unique art style, and the game greatly encapsulates this universe. 7/7",
